{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954215-opinion-on-animal-stats","id":954215,"title":"Opinion on Animal Stats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-19T22:10:02-07:00","id":954215,"title":"Opinion on Animal Stats?","content":"So the animal stats have been vary inconsistent throughout the books, for instance sometimes they stat a gorilla strength 4 and sometimes strength 5 or 6. Sometimes Elephants have strengths of 10, or just 7.<br /> <br /> How do you reconcile this? I'm starting to be won over with the idea of conservative animal stats, after all Exalted has hammered out a finally consistent beastiary in 3rd ed with giant animals using 5 or 7 strength but they can just do certain things easier with their size.<br /> <br /> And Bloodpools for animals? Oyyyyyy!<br /> <br /> Thoughts and advise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:13:58-07:00","id":954430,"title":"","content":"At some point I just ended up just statting them out myself. I wrote some down for various stories, but otherwise I make them up as I go. The books were always kind of shit for consistency (which used to annoy me until I began ignoring them more often).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:03:49-07:00","id":954497,"title":"","content":"I agree, ignore the books, stat them yourself. In general, I use a special Talent, which I label Animal Cunning, to represent relative Intelligence of an animal. Whenever I need to determine if an animal is smart enough, I roll Intelligence (1 for non-kinfolk animals) plus Animal Cunning (0 for insects, 1 amphibians and reptiles, 2 for herbivorous birds and mammals, 3 for carnivorous birds and mammals, 4 for highly intelligent birds and mammals, and 5 for the most intelligent birds and mammals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:50:31-07:00","id":954519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954215-opinion-on-animal-stats?p=954497#post954497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, ignore the books, stat them yourself. In general, I use a special Talent, which I label Animal Cunning, to represent relative Intelligence of an animal. Whenever I need to determine if an animal is smart enough, I roll Intelligence (1 for non-kinfolk animals) plus Animal Cunning (0 for insects, <b>1 amphibians and reptiles</b>, 2 for herbivorous birds and mammals, 3 for carnivorous birds and mammals, 4 for highly intelligent birds and mammals, and 5 for the most intelligent birds and mammals).</div> </div> </div> </div>The triune brain hypothesis is shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:07:53-07:00","id":954566,"title":"","content":"Yes, but amphibians and reptiles are less intelligent than birds and mammals (crocodilians being an obvious exception, and I would give them an Animal Cunning of 3 or 4, depending on the species). When you are dealing with a 6 level scale, you can only do so much gradation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:01:01-07:00","id":954730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/954215-opinion-on-animal-stats?p=954566#post954566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but amphibians and reptiles are less intelligent than birds and mammals (crocodilians being an obvious exception, and I would give them an Animal Cunning of 3 or 4, depending on the species). When you are dealing with a 6 level scale, you can only do so much gradation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an assertion. It was also an assertion that reptiles had uncomplicated brains, but that got shot full of holes in 2005, at the latest, and there was work being done on training turtles and snakes before that, as well of accounts of turtles that were starved for attention and the need to play while they languished to death in zoos (see the work of Burghardt, G.). It was also an assertion that crocs had lungs very different from birds, but that, too, has fallen away, and monitors appear to be getting in on it, too.<br /> <br /> Be careful with assertions. They can lead you far astray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:03:58-07:00","id":955916,"title":"","content":"On a purely mechanical level I'm not fond of a tiger or bear (other than a black bear, anyway) having the same strength as the upper limit of human beings. Brian Shaw's not going to win a wrestling match against a 600 lb. Bengal or 700 lb. grizzly. Likewise wolves being weaker and having less bite damage dice than a German shepherd. (The former has been measured to have twice the bite force of the latter; my understanding is that in previous centuries people who used big dogs to hunt wolves had to employ packs of the former and expect to lose some in every encounter.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:07:27-07:00","id":955950,"title":"","content":"Yes, a tiger can lift a 1000 lbs object with its mouth and leap into a tree. I doubt there is a single human being that could do that. I would give the average tiger Strength 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:35:11-07:00","id":956115,"title":"","content":"Way back, i used to have a written chart (old 3.5 floppy was where i had it), that averaged all the stats from the various books i owned.. Unfortunately i lost it in one of my moves back in the late 90s.. BUT if/when i get back to running VtM or WtA, i would just use THAT splat's book's stats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}